f 17592186045417] [17592186344537 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186343615 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344537 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186343787 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344537 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186343927 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344537 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344537 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344537 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186342257 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344537 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "19c651ff-ec09-54bc-bcdf-8c29a3729b89" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344556 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186342511 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344556 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186342960 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344556 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186343009 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344556 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186343128 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344556 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186344449 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344556 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344556 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344556 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186342511 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344556 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "22e376b5-f6bc-5044-8715-29e828c6d70a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344760 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186342761 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344760 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186342954 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344760 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186343836 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344760 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186344120 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344760 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186344318 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344760 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344760 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344760 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186342761 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344760 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "9ab12311-2d02-5230-960f-45a14af856ac" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345274 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186344537 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345274 #edb/ref 1069 "q-77131" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345274 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345274 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/54/5484647a9c694b95bd9e4b569c84f7263c5e69de5e98f12a1081fd937d298769.png)\n\nWhich of the following is equivalent to the integral ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r,$ where $C$ is the closed polygonal path $KMLK,$ shown in the diagram above, traversed in the **clockwise** direction?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345274 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1a475ad3-f062-505d-a7c3-573f5f8f58ba" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345274 #edb/ref 1074 "First, notice that we can represent $C,$ which is traversed clockwise, as the union of $3$ paths:\n\n$$\nC={C}_{1}\\cup {-{C}_{2}}\\cup {-{C}_{3}},\n$$\n\nwhere $-{C}_{2}$ and $-{C}_{3}$ are the same paths as ${C}_{2}$ and ${C}_{3}$ but traversed in the opposite direction.\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{-{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{-{C}_{3}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r \\\\  & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r-{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r-{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345283 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186344760 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345283 #edb/ref 1069 "q-77180" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345283 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345283 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/93/93c6184f39b28a057866bb02e11e5e81a7abea4ff8a9a907670dd30cfc93d557.png)\n\nThe path ${C}_{1}$ consists of a line segment from the point $A(1,-1)$ to the point $B(1,1),$ and the path ${C}_{2}$ consists of a line segment from the point $B(1,1)$ to the point $O(0,0).$\n\nGiven that ${\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=2,$ evaluate ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r,$ where $F(x,y)=(2x+y)\\,i+(x-2y)\\,j,$ and $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345283 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "616650f8-c315-5a80-80b8-1d1e65ec51b4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345283 #edb/ref 1074 "We will use the fact that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r.\n$$\n\nWe're given the value of the first integral, so we only need to work out the second.\n\nThe path ${C}_{2}$ is the line segment from $B$ to $O.$ It can be parametrized as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{2}(t) & =b+t(0-b) \\\\  & =⟨1,1⟩+t(⟨0,0⟩-⟨1,1⟩) \\\\  & =⟨1-t,1-t⟩ \\\\  & =(1-t)\\,i+(1-t)\\,j,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $0<t<1.$ Along this segment, we have $x=1-t$ and $y=1-t.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F({r}_{2}(t)) & =(2x+y)\\,i+(x-2y)\\,j \\\\  & =(2(1-t)+(1-t))\\,i+((1-t)-2(1-t))\\,j \\\\  & =(3-3t)\\,i+(-1+t)\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the derivative, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{2}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1-t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1-t)j \\\\  & =-i-j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now compute the dot product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F({r}_{2}(t))\\cdot {r}_{2}^{′}(t) & =((3-3t)\\,i+(-1+t)\\,j)\\cdot (-i-j) \\\\  & =-3+3t+1-t \\\\  & =-2+2t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can evaluate the integral, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r \\\\  & =2+{\\int }_{0}^{1}F({r}_{2}(t))\\cdot {r}_{2}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =2+{\\int }_{0}^{1}(-2+2t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =2+(-2t+{t}^{2})\\,{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =2+(1-2) \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345284 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186344556 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345284 #edb/ref 1069 "q-77182" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345284 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345284 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/60/6087da076e65bda5240c428ff67c570ad59ae9a8e5a5a3c9e8406184998de56a.png)\n\nThe path ${C}_{1}$ consists of a the line segment from the point $O(0,0)$ to the point $A(1,0),$ and the path ${C}_{2}$ consists of a line segment from the point $A(1,0)$ to the point $B(0,-2).$\n\nGiven that ${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=\\frac{7}{3},$ evaluate ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r,$ where $F(x,y)=({x}^{2}+y)\\,i+(x-{y}^{2})\\,j,$ and $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345284 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b2144499-6ba0-5eff-ada5-d16752f7b523" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345284 #edb/ref 1074 "We will use the fact that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r.\n$$\n\nWe're given the value of the second integral, so we only need to work out the first.\n\nThe path ${C}_{1}$ is the horizontal line segment from $O$ to $A.$ It can be parametrized as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{1}(t) & =0+t(a-0) \\\\  & =⟨0,0⟩+t(⟨1,0⟩-⟨0,0⟩) \\\\  & =⟨t,0⟩ \\\\  & =t\\,i,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $0<t<1.$ Along this segment, we have $x=t$ and $y=0.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F({r}_{1}(t)) & =({x}^{2}+y)\\,i+(x-{y}^{2})\\,j \\\\  & =({t}^{2}+0)\\,i+(t-{0}^{2})\\,j \\\\  & ={t}^{2}\\,i+t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the derivative, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{1}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(0)j \\\\  & =i\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now compute the dot product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F({r}_{1}(t))\\cdot {r}_{1}^{′}(t) & =({t}^{2}\\,i+t\\,j)\\cdot (i) \\\\  & ={t}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can evaluate the integral, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}F({r}_{1}(t))\\cdot {r}_{1}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t+\\frac{7}{3} \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{t}^{2}\\,\\text{d}t+\\frac{7}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{t}^{3}\\,{|}_{0}^{1}+\\frac{7}{3} \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{3}-0)+\\frac{7}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{7}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424601 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186424623 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424601 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186424624 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424601 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186424625 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424601 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424601 #edb/ref 1045 "Properties of Line Integrals of Vector-Valued Functions" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424601 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186424625 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424601 #edb/ref 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046660 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424601 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186049346 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424601 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "c1a363ff-d156-5c04-b913-8176faf9c905" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424602 #edb/ref 1080 "-{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r-{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424602 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424602 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "09b359e4-02cd-5e97-8b05-35ed5f867cf9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424603 #edb/ref 1080 "32" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424603 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424603 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "23b97760-1703-5852-afc4-69acd21e7cc9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424604 #edb/ref 1080 "{\\int }_{C}{e}^{y+z}\\,\\text{d}x+{e}^{x+z}\\,\\text{d}y+{e}^{x+y}\\,\\text{d}z" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424604 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424604 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "2cf6d6b3-ad5e-5dc6-8ebb-24366de741cb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424605 #edb/ref 1080 "8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424605 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424605 #edb/ref 1083 #